## 1. Where live sessions are tracked

A `Map<string, PtyRecord>` registry in `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:38`, declared next to a `PtyRecord` interface (`ptyManager.ts:21-30`) holding the `IPty` proc, cwd, owner `WebContents`, kind, task/feature ids, and an optional mirror. Entries are added in the three spawn paths (`startDirectPty` at `ptyManager.ts:522`, `startPty` at `ptyManager.ts:645`, `startCommandPty` at `ptyManager.ts:906`) and removed on exit (`ptyManager.ts:551`, `665`, `924`) or via explicit teardown (`teardownRecord()` at `ptyManager.ts:768`, `killAll()` clears the whole map at `ptyManager.ts:814`).

## 2. Resize path

Renderer → IPC → main → pty:
- `src/renderer/terminal/TerminalSessionManager.ts:1002` — `window.electronAPI.ptyResize({ id: this.id, cols, rows: dims.rows })` (with a redundant-resize guard just above it, `:998-999`).
- `src/main/preload.ts:72-73` — bridges to `ipcRenderer.send('pty:resize', args)`.
- `src/main/ipc/ptyIpc.ts:103-111` — `ipcMain.on('pty:resize', ...)` validates args and calls `resizePty`.
- `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:695-705` — the actual apply:
```ts
export function resizePty(id: string, cols: number, rows: number): void {
  const record = ptys.get(id);
  if (record) {
    record.mirror?.resize(cols, rows);
    try {
      record.proc.resize(cols, rows);
    } catch {
      // EBADF can happen during transitions
    }
  }
}
```
It also resizes a headless "mirror" xterm instance to keep serialized state in sync, and swallows `EBADF`.

## 3. Shutdown: SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after 3000ms

`ptyManager.ts:708`: `const GRACEFUL_KILL_TIMEOUT_MS = 3000;`

